      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-03-06_WidnesExaminer_art0063" n="art0063">
        <p>A FEW OUT OF MANY PRESS OPINIONS OF PITTS'S LONDON-ROAD, M ANC H. gSTER, (Just past Station through Railway Arch)</p>
        <p>ALSO AT</p>
        <p>PITTS'S PANTHEON, GAYTHORN, (Just past Manchester Central Station). NEW ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUIDE. WHICH CAN BE HAD GRATIS POST FREE, BY DROPPING US A POST CARD.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S NEW FUKNISHINO GUIDE consists of about 100 large pages and about 1,000 illustrations, though it is not by any mans a complete catalogue of their goods. as such would require a volume ten times the size. It shows plainly Pitts's can bedeck a mansion as well as supply a good and serviceable suit, to the humble cottage, and is certainly worth perusing —l, Oldham Standard."</p>
        <p>PPITTS'S NEW FUttNISHING GUIDE is a work of art, and is illustrated from beginning to end. In it will be found designs of every conceivable descrirtion of furniture suitable for the kitchen, the cottage, the drawing-room, or the mansion, with the prices attached. We need not say that it will be advantageous to become possessed of one.—" Rosseudale Free Press."</p>
        <p>PITTS'S NEW FURNISHING GUIDE contains some of the most impor'ant features of their extensive business. It is admirably arranged and well illustrated,and will itertainly repay a careful perusal, Daily Dispatch."</p>
        <p>PI.TTS'S NEW FURNISHING GUIDE is the right thing in the right place. Excellently got up, it gives sketches and price of every class of furniture, and should be of great value in making a selection to those who are about to set up housekeeping.—" Oldham Chronicle,"</p>
        <p>PITTS'S NEW FURNISHING GUIDE embraces much useful information, and we can thoroughly rec- commend it. Although far from being a complete catalogue of Pitt's immense arock. it will serve as an index to convey to those who peraue it some idea of its magnitude and var- iety. Pitts's are equally well able to furnish a palace or a cottage, and the number of orders the firm have executed for the nobility of the land shows to what extent their rep- utation has exteaded.—"Oheshire Echo".</p>
        <p>PITTS'S NEW FURNISEIING GUIDE is a cora- plete guide to those about to furnish either throughout or in part. The book is profusely illustrated, and practically every item of furniture required for ore's home, however lordly or humble. Is represented in its pages. Another ex- cellent point :is that each Plustaation bears at its foot its price.— ' Rochdale Times".</p>
        <p>11IDITTS'S NEW FURNISHING GUIDE is to hand ii and!a wonderf ally well got up handbook it is. Deal- ing with every furnishing requisite for cottege or ancestral ball and illustrated In the most artistic manner, a perusal of the guide will come sea boon and a blessing to all who are in any doubt as to establishing or improvingithe home. The extent and directness of the contents ena3le the reader to see at a glance how best to spend bis money.—"Blarkpool Times"</p>
        <p>PITTS'S UNRIVALLED HOUSES OF FURNI- PURR at 15i, 22f. 28/. 38/, 5/, 75, 100, 200, up to 1,000 guineas represent the UTKOST POSSIBLE VALUE obtain- able. As compared witla those of'expensive city firms, they are WELL WORTFI DOUBLE our price. Full particulars post free. Cash quotations only. Easy payments ten per cent extra.</p>
        <p>DITTS'S BEDSTEADS AND BEDDING I_ Largest and best selection being cleared Tout at! giving away prices. Rare chance for cheap lines. Da not miss them.</p>
        <p>PITT S'S BASSINETTRS, MAIL CARTS, LAMPS CHINA, GLASS, BARTHBNWARE, INDOOR GAMES, Trunks, Bags, Am.</p>
        <p>SAMUEL PITTS, MANCHESTER LONDON ROAD (Ardwick and Longsight Oars). GATTIRORN (all City Road Oars pass the door). &amp;tab Us bed 1245. (National Telephone 1124.</p>
      </div>
