      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-03-06_WidnesExaminer_art0109" n="art0109">
        <head>ASSOCIATION.</head>
        <p>ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>CHESTER v. NEWTON-LE-WILLOWS.</p>
        <p>These teams met in a combination match at Chester on Saturday afternoon in wet weather and before a good gate. Chester kicked off in drizzling rain. A scrim- mage ensued in the visitors goal, and Rielly scored. Half-time—Chester 1, Newton nil. Final Chester 2, Newton nil.</p>
        <p>EARLESTOWN v. ROCHDALE TOWN. At Earlestown before 500 spectators. The visitors won the toss, and Whitehouse started in a heavy down- pour of rain. Moores scored the visitors' first goal, Partington hitting the ball, and the leather striking the upright entered the net. From a melee in the Roch- dale goal mouth Whitehouse got in a shot which Arrow- smith dropped, although the leather appeared to have rolled over the line the referee ignored the claim for a goal. Just before the interval the visitors' goal was subjected to a severe bombardment, shots being rained in from all quarters, but the nearest attempt at a scot() came from Williamson, who struck the bar from an awkward angle. NVhitehouse obtained the equaliser about a minute before the whistle blew. Half-time— One goal each. Final, Earlestown 2, Rochdale 1. WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT LEAGUE. FIRST DIVISION.</p>
        <p>LATCHFORD BRITANNIA V. WARRINGTON ST. PETER'S</p>
        <p>Played on the ground of the former on Saturday. The home team won easily by six goals to one. LATCHFORD V. RICHMOND'S ATHLETIC.</p>
        <p>Played at Latchford on Saturday, and Latchford were victorious by three goals to one. STOCKTON HEATH V. CABLE CO. ATHLETIC.</p>
        <p>At Stockton Heath on Saturday. Final: Stockton Heath, four goals; Cable, one. "GUARDIAN" V. NICWCHURCH. On the •` Guardian" ground on Saturday. Final: "Guardian" seven goals, Newchurch nil.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-03-06_WidnesExaminer_art0110" n="art0110">
        <head>STOP A COUGH IN ONE NIGHT.</head>
        <p>STOP A COUGH IN ONE NIGHT.</p>
        <p>TAKE VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE. This marvellously successful remedy surpasses anything in the healing art and has the largest sale in the world.</p>
        <p>The remarkable rapidity with which Veno's Lightning Cough Cure absolutely cures the worse cases of COUGHS, COLDS, BRONCHITIS, ASTHMA, INFLUENZA, CATARRH, and CHILDREN'S COUGHS has gained for it scientific recognition throughout the world. GRANVILLE H. SHARPE, F.C.S., Analyst, 11 and 12, Gt. Tower Street, London, says in his certificate of analysis :—" lam of opinion that Veno's Lightning Cough Cure will prove a valuable remedy in the cure of coughs, colds, asthma, and all bronchial complaints." GEO. KNOX, M.D., 256, Second Avenue, Pittsburg, writes :—" Veno's Lightning Couqh Cure excels in chronic coughsand bronchitis, and is especially good for children." Ask for Veno's LIGHTNING COUGH CURE at Chemists,price Is. lid. and 2s. 9d., or post free from the Veno Drug Co., Hulme, Manchester.</p>
