        <p>Sworn Statament. "I, Frances Butterfield, of 84, Victoria Road, Mexboro,' Yorkshire, do solemnly and sincerely declare as follows :—['or forty years I suffered from indigestion, that is to say from the time I was a child under ten years of age until I was well through my forty-ninth year. During nearly the whole of that time I had suffered from biliousness, so badly as to cause vomiting of bile at intervals, usuallyof two or three days,and scarcely ever less frequently than once a fortnight. I then suffered so very acutely as to be repeatedly picaed up from the floor where I had fallen powerless through the exhaustion 'mused by the vomiting. I was attended by doctors, who failed to cure me, and in the course of years I have consumed hundreds of boxes and bottles of various medicines without effect. Fifteen months previous to this date I commenced to take Bile Beans. In less than three months Bile Beans completely cured me, and I have not had indi- gestion or biliousness since. My appetite has become good, I now enjoy my sleep, and during the whole of the last twelve Months, since I was cured by Bile Beans, I have enjoyed excellent health. Nothing but Bile Beans cured me. Bile Beans also cured my son, Arrowsmith Butterfield, aged fifteen, of skin eruptions of a most severe character, and nervousness and weakness. They restored him to he:ath and strength after he had been] reduced to almost fieshlessness. And I make this solemn deolaration conscienti- oudy believing the same to be true, and by virtue of the Statutary Declaration Act, 1835. (Signed) Frances Butterfield. Declared by the said Frances Butterfield at Alexborough, in the County of York, this, the second day of January, 1903, before me, FREDK. E. HALL, A Commissioner to Administer Oaths.</p>
